<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="h-100">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>GeoRoadbook — create your geocaching roadbook</title>
    <meta name="description" content="GeoRoadbook is a free and open source web app to create your geocaching roadbook ready-to-print from your gpx file (Pocket queries, GSAK, GCTour, etc.)">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/design/icon-roadbook.png">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,600;0,700;1,600&family=DM+Sans:wght@300;400;500&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    {% block javascripts %}
        {% block importmap %}{{ importmap('app') }}{% endblock %}
    {% endblock %}
</head>
<body class="d-flex flex-column h-100">

    <header>
        <nav class="navbar">
            <div class="container">
                <span class="navbar-brand-name">◎ GeoRoadbook</span>
                <div>
                    {% if app.user is empty %}
                        <a href="{{ path('app_login') }}" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Sign in</a>
                    {% else %}
                        <div class="hello-user">
                            <img src="{{ app.user.avatarUrl }}" loading="lazy" width="28" alt="{{ app.user.username }}'s avatar">
                            <span>{{ app.user.username }}</span>
                            <a href="{{ path('app_logout') }}" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Sign out</a>
                        </div>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </div>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="flex-shrink-0">
        <div class="container">
            {% if exception is defined %}
                <div class="alert alert-danger mt-3" role="alert">
                    <strong>{{ exception.type }}:</strong> {{ exception.message }} (Code: {{ exception.code }})
                </div>
            {% endif %}
            {% block main %}{% endblock %}
        </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer mt-auto">
        <div class="container">
            <ul>
                <li><i class="bi bi-question-circle"></i> <a href="#faq" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i> <a href="#about" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#about">About</a></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-github"></i> <a href="https://github.com/Surfoo/georoadbook" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </footer>

    {# FAQ Modal #}
    <div id="faq" class="modal fade" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h4 class="modal-title">FAQ</h4>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <dl>
                        <dt>My language isn't in the list, how to get it?</dt>
                        <dd>You can translate <a href="https://github.com/Surfoo/georoadbook/blob/master/app/locales/en.xml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">this file</a> and make a pull request on GitHub or send it by email.</dd>

                        <dt>Why does my roadbook no longer exist?</dt>
                        <dd>All roadbooks are kept 1 month after the last modification date. You can see the date by hovering on the "Save" button — saving resets the timer.</dd>

                        <dt>Is my roadbook public and published on the internet?</dt>
                        <dd>No, your roadbook is absolutely private and does not appear on search engines. Only you know the link. Your roadbook can't be found by guessing the URL — there are 16<sup>16</sup> possibilities.</dd>

                        <dt>Why doesn't my GPX file work?</dt>
                        <dd>Only GPX files with version 1.0.1 are supported. If you don't know the version, <a href="https://www.geocaching.com/account/settings/preferences" target="_blank" rel="noopener">check your preferences</a>. GPX files with tracks are not supported. If your file still doesn't work, it may be corrupted.</dd>

                        <dt>Why can't I see spoilers in the roadbook?</dt>
                        <dd>Links to spoilers aren't included in the GPX file. To include them, insert them manually or use <a href="http://spoilers4gpx.vaguelibre.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spoilers4gpx</a>.</dd>

                        <dt>Why is pagination missing in the table of contents?</dt>
                        <dd>WebKit doesn't implement this feature yet. Set pagination manually after a first PDF export, or use Print Preview in Chrome.</dd>

                        <dt>Why does my roadbook look good in the editor but not in the PDF?</dt>
                        <dd>The PDF rendering is great but some HTML/CSS features aren't fully implemented yet.</dd>

                        <dt>I have a problem with GeoRoadbook, what can I do?</dt>
                        <dd>If you find bugs, please <a href="https://github.com/Surfoo/georoadbook/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open an issue on GitHub</a>, or contact me by email.</dd>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# About Modal #}
    <div id="about" class="modal fade" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg">
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h4 class="modal-title">About</h4>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">
                    <h5>Attribution</h5>
                    <p>
                        <span style="float: right; padding: 0 0 0 12px;">
                            <a href="https://www.geocaching.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                                <img src="/design/live.png" alt="Geocaching API">
                            </a>
                        </span>
                        Powered by the Geocaching API. Made possible through the support of Geocaching Premium Memberships,
                        the API program gives third-party developers the opportunity to work with Geocaching HQ on a full suite
                        of integrated products and services for the community. API developer applications are designed to work
                        with the core services of geocaching.com and provide additional features to the geocaching community.<br><br>
                        Geocaching Cache Type Icons © Groundspeak, Inc. DBA Geocaching HQ. All rights reserved. Used with Permission.
                    </p>

                    <h5>Privacy Policy</h5>
                    <p>
                        GeoRoadbook collects some information about the connected user in order to keep them connected with a session cookie.<br>
                        GeoRoadbook collects your Pocket Queries if you are connected and a premium member.<br>
                        GeoRoadbook does not share any of your personal data with third parties.<br>
                        Your created roadbooks are deleted after 30 days without modifications. You can exercise your data rights by sending the roadbook URL to delete by email (see below).
                    </p>

                    <h5>Contact</h5>
                    <p>For questions, bugs, or suggestions: <strong>surfooo at gmail dot com</strong> (French or English only)</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {% block body_scripts %}{% endblock %}

</body>
</html>
